{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1392126-qc-jahanara-the-celestial-admiral-of-the-dreaming-sea","id":1392126,"title":"[QC] Jahanara, the Celestial Admiral of the Dreaming Sea","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-27T22:41:36-07:00","id":1392126,"title":"[QC] Jahanara, the Celestial Admiral of the Dreaming Sea","content":"<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/17bNF8txsAQdcitzCWe58zIbnHqWY9B3upHmJlYgZIsU/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Link to the Google Document</a><br /> <br /> In a game I'm running set in the empire of Prasad, I mentioned Jahanara, the Celestial Admiral in passing as a deity. I've been listening to Journey to the West and I decided to write a quick character for including her.<br /> <br /> This is the first quick character I've written, so I am very interested in feedback!<br /> <br /> To entice, here's one of her charms:<br /> <b>Perilous Seafoam Blockade</b> <i>(20m, 1wp; Simple; Indefinite; Essence 5) </i><br /> Jahanara must appear before the rulers or administrators of a coastal city in order to use this charm. She declares a transgression they have made against her, or offers the terms under which they may surrender. If they refuse her offer or demands, she may activate this charm.<br /> The coastal city suddenly becomes nearly impossible for any ship to enter or leave. Any ship that attempts to do so must succeed on a difficulty 7 (Wits + Sail) roll to navigate the sudden, impossibly sharp waves that emerge to push the ship back from where it came. Failure to avoid this hazard causes the ship to take three points of hull damage and be either forced back into the city\u2019s harbor, or left adrift in the ocean several miles from the city.<br /> Those who avoid this gauntlet find that they are pursued by a ship made of white sea-foam and manned by strange, many armed crab women. This ship has the statistics of an imperial trireme; Jahanara may treat it as though she currently commanded it, including using her other charms that modify naval combat actions on it. For the purposes of boarding actions, treat the sailors aboard the ship as if they were a size 2 battle-group of Lintha Reavers (Corebook, page 397), with average drill and one Might.<br /> <hr /><br /> I am particularly interested in balance; if she would be an interesting or fair combatant. I also want to know if I'm hitting the right level for an essence 6 god, or if I need to tune down or tune up, or revise her as an essence five deity.<br /> <br /> I already have plans for discussing ways to introduce and use her in play, but I was hoping to get some feedback first.<br /> <br /> Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4578-zale","name":"Zale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4578_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-28T00:34:14-07:00","id":1392139,"title":"","content":"It looks really good.<br /> <br /> Balanced against other NPCs it's pretty perfect.<br /> <br /> A few minor points:<br /> <br /> Invested Solar sailors throwing 20+ successes on a Sail roll is a thing that happens.<br /> <br /> You may want to up her Sail pool to 14 and give her a way to do stuff even if she loses the roll off (like an uncontested free Positioning Stratagem each turn).<br /> <br /> Likewise, her combat abilities are exactly where they should be for a god of this level. Meaning your Solar/Lunar party is going to roflstomp her.<br /> <br /> Not a PC, but it'd still be nice to see at least one negative Intimacy: maybe pirates or the undead.<br /> <br /> Other than that... very nice indeed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/>